     "file": "gekr113",
     "pages": 3,
     "head": "13 Awadh. His father was the famous Kalka Prasad and uncle Binda Deen, who consolidated the Lucknow Gharana of Kathak. Trained under his uncle Binda Deen. Later, he established a post-independence with his elder brother Acchan Maharaj repetorrie of dance. He made his debut in Lucknow in 1926 at the All India Music Conference after which he performed regularly as a soloist, and with his elder brothers Acchan and Lacchu Maharaj. He moved to Delhi in 1955 and taught Kathak at the Shriram Bharatiya Kala Kendra, establishing the tradition of the Lucknow Gharana in Delhi. He was very famous for his abhinaya and bhav batana, and he performed such in the court style of sitting and enacting. He taught his nephew, the famous Birju Maharaj and many other famous Kathak dancers of India. He is survived by his sons Ram Mohan and Kishan Mohan who are also accomplished dancers, and gurus. He was the rec"
