     "pages": 10,
     "head": "19 the ART OF CALLIGRAPHY Scripts have the power to record people’s languages and expressions. India’s writing systems can be traced from the 5000-year old Indus-Sarasvati civilisation. But the earliest decoded inscriptions in Brahmi script from the Ashokan edicts are almost 2300 years old. The original Constitution of India was handwritten by two expert calligraphers. Prem Behari Narain Raizada wrote the English version and Vasant Krishan Vaidya wrote it in Hindi. It was signed on 26 January 1950, the day we observe as Republic Day. Today, the Indian constitution officially recognises 22 languages. Look at the beautiful forms and variations in Indian scripts in the tree on the left. 19_Visual Arts.indd 19419_Visual Arts.indd 194 11-04-2025 12:04:3011-04-2025 12:04:30 Reprint 2026-27"
